[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4024518840","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/117254#issuecomment-4024518840","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117254","id":4024518840,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7v4Ui4","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-09T15:18:36Z","updated_at":"2026-03-09T15:18:36Z","body":"Currently, there's no menu accelerators set at all (the feature itself should be supported, so it should be fixable). Not sure if adding `Alt+Letter` shortcuts to open menus won't conflict with existing shortcuts.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4024518840/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4029370734","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/117254#issuecomment-4029370734","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117254","id":4029370734,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7wK1Fu","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-10T07:48:16Z","updated_at":"2026-03-10T07:48:16Z","body":"> menus in the menu bar don't read\n\nI assume you mean menu names, which happens because unlike a native menu Godot menu automatically opens newly selected menu and focused on the first items.\n\n> accelerator\n\nJust to be clear, by accelerators do you mean single letter shortcuts used after menu is opened with the ALT or shortcuts (like Ctrl+S), it seems to be used in both contexts.\n\n- Godot menus allow searching for menu item by typing the start of the item name while menu is open, but not ALT+letter.\n- Shortcuts (like Ctrl+S) are set for common menu items and do work, but are not read by the screen reader when item is selected. Support for shortcut information is not fully implemented in AccessKit, but probably can be worked around by adding it to the item name.\n\n> alt-f/p\n\nMost of the ALT+Letter shortcuts are already used for various other purposes, so there's no way to use it by default (but it should be possible to make it configurable).\n\n> Ideally, this would be pulled up with alt\n\nThis can be done, but Godot interface can have multiple menu bars at the same time (e.g., main and script editor menu).","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4029370734/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4029386237","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/117254#issuecomment-4029386237","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117254","id":4029386237,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7wK439","user":{"login":"ethindp","id":8030501,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgwMzA1MDE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8030501?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ethindp","html_url":"https://github.com/ethindp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ethindp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ethindp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ethindp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ethindp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ethindp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ethindp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ethindp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ethindp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ethindp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-10T07:51:43Z","updated_at":"2026-03-10T07:51:43Z","body":"> Just to be clear, by accelerators do you mean single letter shortcuts used after menu is opened with the ALT or shortcuts (like Ctrl+S), it seems to be used in both contexts.\n\nI mean things like using alt-p to get to the project menu.\n\n> Most of the ALT+Letter shortcuts are already used for various other purposes, so there's no way to use it by default (but it should be possible to make it configurable).\n\nAh, not really sure how best to approach solving that; I didn't know this.\n\n> This can be done, but Godot interface can have multiple menu bars at the same time (e.g., main and script editor menu).\n\nWell... That's going to be interesting. Godot would be the first app I've ever used with a contextual menu bar, assuming we choose that route. Although that would be confusing and it may be better to split the script editor into a separate window at that point maybe?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4029386237/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4029398143","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/117254#issuecomment-4029398143","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117254","id":4029398143,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7wK7x_","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-10T07:54:34Z","updated_at":"2026-03-10T07:54:34Z","body":"> Although that would be confusing and it may be better to split the script editor into a separate window at that point maybe?\n\nIt is detachable as a separate window (a lot of editor parts are), but by default it is embedded.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4029398143/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4029409247","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/117254#issuecomment-4029409247","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117254","id":4029409247,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7wK-ff","user":{"login":"ethindp","id":8030501,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgwMzA1MDE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8030501?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ethindp","html_url":"https://github.com/ethindp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ethindp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ethindp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ethindp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ethindp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ethindp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ethindp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ethindp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ethindp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ethindp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"pub